  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: timing side-channel in RSA-PSK ClientKeyExchange\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2023-5981-pre1.patch: use the appropriate level of\n       randomness for each nettle operation and fail through the library\n       state instead of abort(), in lib/nettle/pk.c, lib/fips.h,\n       lib/includes/gnutls/crypto.h.\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2023-5981-pre2.patch: add the side-channel silent\n       gnutls_privkey_decrypt_data2() on top of nettle rsa_sec_decrypt(), in\n       lib/gnutls_privkey.c, lib/nettle/pk.c, lib/pkcs11_privkey.c,\n       configure.ac and related headers, with selftest and test.\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2023-5981.patch: use the new function in the\n       RSA-PSK server without branching on the decryption result, in\n       lib/auth/rsa_psk.c.\n     - debian/libgnutls30.symbols: add gnutls_privkey_decrypt_data2.\n     - debian/control: build-depend on nettle-dev with rsa_sec_decrypt.\n     - CVE-2023-5981\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: incomplete fix for CVE-2023-5981\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2024-0553.patch: move the PSK lookup and key\n       setup before the decryption, in lib/auth/rsa_psk.c.\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-5260-decrypt_data2.patch: reject a\n       ciphertext that does not match the modulus size and size the PKCS#11\n       buffer for the plaintext, in lib/auth/rsa_psk.c and\n       lib/pkcs11_privkey.c.\n     - CVE-2024-0553",
